<title>SOUTH KOREA: Halla in car parts deal with GM.</title>
<headline>Halla in car parts deal with GM.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Halla Climate Control Corp said on Tuesday it has agreed to join General Motors Corp's project to develop new medium-sized sedans.</p>
<p>A Halla statement said the company would develop and supply air-conditioners and heaters for GM's new vehicles.</p>
<p>But it gave no further details.</p>
<p>Seperately, Halla has won an order to supply about $20 million worth of car air-conditioner parts to Taiwan Auto Air Corp over the next five years. Halla would also provide the Taiwanese firm with air-conditioner manufacturing technology.</p>
<p>Halla Climate is a 50-50 joint venture between Ford Motor Co and South Korea's Mando Machinery Corp.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
